      "rank": 2,
      "content_hash": "94ba485f3fbc3025a5c2215fe1c0637bb149648edfbcc1d0b8ffbcc61d24a0fe",
      "content": "# dbt connection refused — version 1 — 2026-10-20\nSymptoms: connection_refused, connection refused, dbt_orders, dbt_run.\nConfirm: failed task log and selected dbt artifacts identify the failing connection. mcp_readonly success only confirms that separate connection.\nAction: developer checks dbt endpoint, service availability, routing and authentication using explicitly supplied configuration. Do not expose passwords. Correct a port only if endpoint evidence proves it is wrong.\nPrerequisite: establish the actual dbt execution configuration; do not infer an incorrect port from a generic refusal.\nVerification: successful new pipeline execution and passing not_null/unique checks; a successful connection probe alone does not prove recovery.\nExclude: schema and data-quality failures with functioning connectivity. Never claim a specific port from an absent log value.\n",
      "method": "lexical_overlap_checkpoint"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "rb-quality",
      "doc_version": "1",
      "chunk_id": "rb-quality:whole",
      "rank": 3,
      "content_hash": "9642f10da53b0c8ed050f0a1a9e9e928059f5d812aeeb7e40735ae0ebc0477f4",
      "content": "# Null order key — version 1 — 2026-10-20\nSymptoms: not_null, order_id, null rows, dbt_test.\nConfirm: selected invocation records failing not_null_order_id; current raw.orders profile provides null_counts and limited samples. Do not treat current counts as past counts.\nAction: developer verifies source provenance, repairs the source mapping or quarantines invalid records according to the agreed policy, preserving originals.\nPrerequisite: confirm business key definition and approved remediation policy.\nVerification: separate new execution succeeds, not_null and unique both pass, reconciled counts and aggregates are checked.\nExclude: absent column or failed connectivity; a retry alone cannot repair bad data.\n",
      "method": "lexical_overlap_checkpoint"
    }
